{"course": {"schema_version": "1.0", "course_id": "mitocw-15-310-spring-2003", "institution": "Massachusetts Institute of Technology", "platform": "MIT OpenCourseWare", "course_codes": ["15.310"], "cross_listed_codes": ["15.301"], "course_title": "Managerial Psychology Laboratory", "course_slug": "15-310-managerial-psychology-laboratory-spring-2003", "term": "Spring", "year": 2003, "as_taught_in": "Spring 2003", "language": "en", "departments": ["Sloan School of Management"], "academic_levels": ["Graduate"], "instructors": ["Prof. Dan Ariely", "Prof. Tom Allen"], "subject_primary": "Management", "subject_secondary": ["Organizational Behavior", "Social Science", "Psychology"], "topic_tree": [{"name": "Business", "subtopics": [{"name": "Management", "specialties": []}, {"name": "Organizational Behavior", "specialties": []}]}, {"name": "Social Science", "subtopics": [{"name": "Psychology", "specialties": []}]}], "topic_keywords": [], "pedagogy_tags": [], "assessment_types": [], "course_feature_tags": ["Activity Assignments", "Lecture Notes", "Presentation Assignments", "Projects", "Written Assignments"], "description": "Surveys social psychology and organization theory interpreted in the context of the managerial environment. Shares lectures with 15.301, with a separate recitation required. 15.301 is intended primarily for non-Sloan students, both graduate and undergraduate. Deals with a number of diverse subjects, including motivation and reward systems for engineers and scientists in industry; the aging of technical groups; the management of R&D matrix organizations; and the architecture of R&D laboratories and its effect on communication patterns in the organization. 15.301 is a core subject for students majoring in management science. A laboratory is a required element of the course for these students. It involves projects of an applied nature in behavioral science. Emphasizes use of behavioral science research methods to test hypotheses concerning organizational b